WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:13.700
87. Stuttering. Stuttering, also called stammering, is a communication disorder.

2
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.260
People who stutter have a very difficult time speaking. When they try to talk, they seem

3
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:25.060
to get stuck on words or sounds. They may repeat the beginning sound of a word many

4
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:33.500
times as in, my n-n-name is. Or they may make the same sound for a long time before they

5
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:42.040
are able to say the word as in, my n-n-name is. They may also have trouble making any

6
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:48.240
sound at all when they talk. Stuttering is still a mysterious problem. It affects more

7
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:56.340
boys than girls. It usually becomes obvious at a young age soon after a child starts talking.

8
00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:02.580
One cause of stuttering seems to be genetic. However, not all stutterers have the stuttering

9
00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:10.320
gene. It may also be caused by trauma early in life or other factors in a child's development.

10
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:17.700
Most children outgrow stuttering, but for some people, the problem continues into adulthood.

11
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:24.780
Stuttering is not a consistent problem. It gets better or worse depending on the situation.

12
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:30.300
Singing often reduces stuttering, while public speaking or even talking on the phone can

13
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:37.080
make it much worse. Stuttering causes a lot of emotional stress.

14
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:43.600
Stutterers may feel tense and anxious in social situations or ashamed of the way they speak.

15
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.820
This causes some stutterers to stay away from other people, which can lead to loneliness

16
00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:56.900
and depression. Now people are accepting stuttering more, and stutterers are becoming less ashamed.

17
00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:02.860
There are many famous people who have stuttered. King George VI of England, for example, and

18
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:09.620
Lewis Carroll, who wrote Alice in Wonderland. Even Julia Roberts stuttered at one point.

19
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:15.420
There's even a Facebook page for stutterers to join. Sounding different shouldn't mean

20
00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.020
you can't communicate.
